{"nodes": [{"id": "ipqc_html", "label": "ipqc.html", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "ipqc.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "ipqc_rationale_changes", "label": "ipqc.html changes vs original Apps Script", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "ipqc.html", "source_location": "lines 13-44", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ipqc.html replaces legacy Ipqc.html + IpqcCheckpoint.js, covering only the inspector's checkpoint-submission screen (QC manager/standards/NCP screens are out of scope, deferred to qc-manager.html). Changes: (1) original had to prompt the inspector to type their own email (localStorage-saved modal) because Google Apps Script's Session.getActiveUser() only returns email for users with script-edit rights \u2014 regular staff got blank. Now Supabase Auth provides a real logged-in identity, so the self-declare modal is dropped entirely \u2014 an improvement in identity trustworthiness, not a feature cut. (2) Evidence photos: original uploaded base64 to Apps Script which wrote to Google Drive (_uploadIpqcEvidence_); now the browser uploads directly to Supabase Storage bucket 'ipqc-evidence' (created in migration_phase_D0_foundation.sql), gets a public URL, and passes the URL array into duc_submit_ipqc_check via p_anh_urls, per the design recorded in migration_phase4_step4. (3) The inspection queue (formerly getIpqcQueue_) filters to the 'currently active id_dong' per machine including paired molds; no existing public RPC/view covers this exactly (duc_get_ipqc_due_by_id_dong from step9 only serves the dashboard badge and excludes not-yet-due checkpoints, which the queue needs to show as 'upcoming') \u2014 so this page reads duc_ca_hien_tai + duc_ipqc_checkpoint directly (both have public read RLS) and computes the active-id_dong set client-side, replicating server logic _getActiveIdDongSet_ (latest row_seq per machine plus paired rows via khuon_kep_voi). (4) Business-rule validation (OK requires all-pass; NG/warning requires >=1 fail plus mandatory note) was re-added server-side inside duc_submit_ipqc_check itself (migration_phase4_step12), since the public RPC is called directly by the browser and can no longer rely solely on trusted Apps Script server-side checks."}, {"id": "ipqc_loadqueue", "label": "loadQueue()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "ipqc.html", "source_location": "line 284", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "ipqc_getactiveiddongset", "label": "getActiveIdDongSet()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "ipqc.html", "source_location": "line 257", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "ipqc_renderqueue", "label": "renderQueue()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "ipqc.html", "source_location": "line 338", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "ipqc_opencheck", "label": "openCheck()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "ipqc.html", "source_location": "line 362", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "ipqc_uploadevidencephotos", "label": "uploadEvidencePhotos()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "ipqc.html", "source_location": "line 473", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "ipqc_submitcheck", "label": "submitCheck()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "ipqc.html", "source_location": "line 492", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "ipqc_startpolling", "label": "startPolling() (ipqc)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "ipqc.html", "source_location": "line 324", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "rpc_duc_submit_ipqc_check", "label": "RPC duc_submit_ipqc_check", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "ipqc